# Distributable archives live at the repo root. Mark them binary so no
# line-ending conversion can ever corrupt the archive on checkout.
# (Git usually auto-detects binary content, but for a file developers download
# and run, being explicit is worth the one line.)
*.zip binary

# Orchestration kit: append-only loop state merges cleanly in parallel runs,
# and the loop drivers must check out with the endings their interpreters need.
_goals/LEARNINGS.md merge=union
_goals/ESCALATIONS.md merge=union
_goals/*/orchestration-log.md merge=union
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Task 00's golden regression baseline is LF-only by construction. Without
# this, core.autocrlf=true checks it out as CRLF (2045 bytes vs the committed
# 2000), and task 05's AC1 diff against it fails on every Windows clone for a
# reason unrelated to billing.
tests/golden/** -text

# The deploy/ hooks are MDM-pushed to machines whose interpreter (a fleet
# shebang, or a Windows py launcher) needs the endings below - without this a
# macOS/Linux fleet machine gets a CRLF shebang line and the hook fails to
# execute, silently, because it is required to exit 0.
deploy/*.py text eol=lf
